  "statement": "A truck can carry at most W kilograms. There are n parcels; parcel i weighs w_i kilograms and is worth v_i euros. Choose a set of parcels whose total weight is at most W and whose total worth is as large as possible. Each parcel is taken whole or left.\n\nInput: the first line holds n and W (1 <= n <= 100, 1 <= W <= 10^9). Each of the next n lines holds w_i v_i (1 <= w_i <= 10^9, 1 <= v_i <= 1000).\nOutput: one line with the largest total worth that fits (0 when no parcel fits).\n\nW and the weights are far too large for a table indexed by weight, and trying every subset is too slow.\n\nExample\nInput:\n3 8\n3 30\n4 50\n5 60\nOutput:\n90\n(parcels 1 and 3 weigh 8 and are worth 90)",
  "starter_code": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    long long W;\n    cin >> n >> W;\n    vector<long long> w(n), v(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> w[i] >> v[i];\n    // Print the best total worth\n}\n",
  "time_limit_ms": 1000,
  "memory_limit_mb": 256,
  "comparator": "trim",
  "timer_seconds": 1500,
